  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Hospice Africa Uganda Palliative Care for people living with HIV and AIDS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project continues the cancer and HIV &amp; AIDS palliative care (PC) activities that Hospice Africa Uganda has been conducting since 1993, in its three project sites of Hospice Africa Kampala, Mobile Hospice Mbarara and Little Hospice Hoima. It aims to comprehensively reduce the impact of HIV in its three project sites by improving access to quality HIV prevention and care and support for direct beneficiaries and affected family members and communities. It will: 

&#x2022;	Provide free essential drugs for pain relief and symptom control for adults and children living with HIV and HIV-related cancers;
&#x2022;	Provide transport to enable PC provision in a range of settings and to support end of life care for programme beneficiaries;
&#x2022;	Continue its national PC advocacy, to reposition pain and symptom management and end-of-life care within the overall health and HIV &amp; AIDS care system;
&#x2022;	Provide support for Orphans and Vulnerable Children living with and affected by HIV &amp; AIDS and Cancer</narrative>
  </description>
